et its subsidiary  calibre manage libra for facebook users  and facebook executives have stated that  calibre will not share account holders  purchase information with facebook  without authorization  however the system is also planned to  include a friend finder search function  and the use of this function will  constitute permission for calibre to  combine the account holders transaction  history with their facebook account  libra will not rely on cryptocurrency  mining  only members of the libra association  will be able to process transactions via  the permissioned blockchain  libra hopes to begin transitioning to a  permissionless proof-of-stake system  within five years  although their own materials admit that  no solution exists that can deliver the  scale stability and security needed to  support billions of people and  transactions across the globe through a  permissionless network  libra's source code is written in rust  and published as open source under the  apache license with the launch on the  18th of june 2019  elenu an opinion writer at bloomberg  news tried compiling and running the  publicly released code for libra  as supplied the software did little more  than allow fake coins to be put in a  wallet  almost all of the white paper  functionality is not implemented  including major architectural features  that have yet to be invented  who was surprised that facebook would  release software in such a state  facebook plans to release a digital  wallet called calibre in 2020  made available in messenger whatsapp as  well as in a standalone app  move is the libra blockchain's proposed  smart contract and custom transactions  language  compiled to bytecode  how this all plays out remains to be  seen  but given the success of crypto  currencies and the strong networking  communications of the social media giant  the pairing is poised for success  as long as the public at large keeps  clicking that ever so prominent like  button
 

